as not going to be  there  so i really didn't know what to do and  when i announced it on thursday i had  nothing planned for  you know friday saturday sunday monday  also out of respect  for the queen's funeral coming up and i  just said well let's just see how it all  plays out at least it gives some people  um advanced notice before the labor cup  that i was going to be here and it gives  me a chance at the labor cup to see the  the crowd see the fans be surrounded by  um  by all the greatest players and uh have  a great time and have fun because that's  what i wanted to be  first of all serena  now you  it is the end of an era what have you  both brought to the sport do you think  different things for sure you know but  at the end we both did it as moms and  dads you know  funny to think think of that because uh  both when we were young made it on tour  and never thought we're probably going  to end as  as that at the end um i think we were  definitely the bridge you know for a  very long time from the old generation  to the new generation which i think  has been a privilege for me to play  across generations like this same for  her um  and she brought the power game in like  no other so she's been obviously  instrumental with that and being um a  game changer is something um  that i think  is the ultimate compliment i don't know  if i did that in any way but i did it my  way and i i hope people enjoy watching  me play for so long and  i know we'll always would love to return  to tennis in some shape or form but i  don't know in which capacity but i loved  my my life on tour and i can't thank  the people enough for all their support  throughout the years
 

